# Copy to holdings.csv and fill in. synthesize-finance.py reads holdings.csv
# only — this .example file is never loaded, so a half-filled template can
# never quietly become "your portfolio" in a brief.
#
# Only `symbol` is required. Every other column sharpens the ranking:
#   status   — held | watch | exited. 'watch' items get flagged on triggers
#              without being treated as exposure you already carry.
#   stage    — Asset Revesting stage 1-4 (accumulation/markup/distribution/decline)
#              if you track it; blank is fine.
#   weight_pct — share of portfolio. Drives how hard news on it is surfaced.
#   stop     — stop-loss level, if any. News near a stop is worth more.
#   note     — free text, e.g. the condition you're waiting on.
#
# Nothing here is sent anywhere except into the local Claude CLI call that
# writes your brief.
symbol,status,weight_pct,stage,cost_basis,stop,note
QQQ,held,25,,,,
BIL,held,65,,,,cash equivalent
USO,watch,10,,,,conditional entry — not yet opened
